  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v6.0.0 — the health data types move to Kebechet.Types.Health, a package without MAUI, under its own namespaces.\n\nBREAKING CHANGES\n• Namespaces (#62): DTOs, enums, results and their helpers are now in Kebechet.Types.Health.* — replace using Maui.Health.Models with using Kebechet.Types.Health.Models (same for .Enums, .Extensions, .Constants).\n\nNEW\n• Kebechet.Types.Health (#62): the DTOs, enums and results as a plain .NET package, for code shared with a watch app or a backend.\n• HealthDataSdk.GoogleHealthServices (#62): marks workouts recorded on a Wear OS watch with Health Services.\n\nCHANGED\n• WorkoutSession (#62): its constructor and the DTO-to-permission helpers are public, so other health libraries can use them.\n\nPREVIOUS RELEASE — v5.1.0: a read refused because the app is in the background is reported, not logged as an error.\n\nNEW\n• Read results carry a typed Error (#58): ReadHealthDataError.BackgroundReadNotPermitted marks a read Health Connect refuses while the app is in the background.\n\nCHANGED\n• Android (#58): a read Health Connect refuses or limits in the background returns BackgroundReadNotPermitted and is logged as information, not as an error.",
